  'sushiswap',
  '{"success_factors_missing":["no_liquidity_moat","declining_volume"],"forensic_analysis":{"version":"forensic-analysis-v1","outcome":{"label":"declining","summary":"Sushi remains operational but its owned-pool capital base is severely diminished. The research snapshot records about 32.96 million dollars of TVL versus a roughly 7.04 billion dollar peak, a 99.53 percent drawdown, with about 21.79 million dollars of 30-day SushiSwap-adapter volume.","confidence":"high","as_of":"2026-07-29","source_refs":["https://api.llama.fi/protocol/sushiswap","https://api.llama.fi/summary/dexs/sushiswap?excludeTotalDataChart=false&excludeTotalDataChartBreakdown=false&dataType=dailyVolume","https://www.banqueducanada.ca/wp-content/uploads/2024/07/sdp2024-12.pdf"]},"why":{"summary":"Sushi states that it lost operational efficiency and long-term focus after leadership departure, experienced internal power struggles, and became a shell of its earlier position. Those disruptions coincided with a near-total owned-pool TVL drawdown. Sushi responded by shifting toward routing and aggregation across more than forty chains, but current first-party liquidity remains small. No credible source apportions the decline among leadership churn, incentive-driven liquidity, competition, market contraction, and product sprawl, so causal confidence is medium.","confidence":"medium","source_refs":["https://www.sushi.com/blog/introducing-sushi-head-chef-jared-grey","https://api.llama.fi/protocol/sushiswap","https://www.sushi.com/blog/rp7","https://darcyallen.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/02/allen-berg-lane-treasury-governance-dilemma.pdf","https://www.banqueducanada.ca/wp-content/uploads/2024/07/sdp2024-12.pdf"]},"strategic_choices":[{"decision":"Launch through a liquidity-mining strategy that moved liquidity from Uniswap and rapidly expanded the SUSHI-governed fork.","consequence":"Sushi briefly overtook Uniswap in TVL and established a major brand quickly, but the initial liquidity advantage did not become a durable moat.","confidence":"medium","source_refs":["https://www.sushi.com/blog/introducing-sushi-head-chef-jared-grey","https://api.llama.fi/protocol/sushiswap","https://darcyallen.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/02/allen-berg-lane-treasury-governance-dilemma.pdf"]},{"decision":"Expand into many products and chains, then pivot the user experience toward Route Processor aggregation that sources external liquidity.","consequence":"Sushi can offer routes across more than forty chains even where its own pools are thin. Aggregator reach therefore must not be presented as recovery of Sushi-owned liquidity.","confidence":"high","source_refs":["https://www.sushi.com/blog/swap-anything","https://www.sushi.com/blog/rp7","https://api.llama.fi/protocol/sushiswap"]},{"decision":"Use team-led operations and treasury and operations multisigs while reserving major restructuring for community votes.","consequence":"The model permits faster day-to-day execution, but business strategy and treasury operations remain concentrated among team members and multisig signers. Sushi associates earlier leadership discontinuity and power struggles with loss of focus.","confidence":"high","source_refs":["https://www.sushi.com/faq/governance/governance/sushi-governance","https://www.sushi.com/blog/introducing-sushi-head-chef-jared-grey","https://darcyallen.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/02/allen-berg-lane-treasury-governance-dilemma.pdf","https://www.banqueducanada.ca/wp-content/uploads/2024/07/sdp2024-12.pdf"]},{"decision":"Redirect all xSushi protocol fees to the treasury through Kanpai during a treasury drawdown.","consequence":"Sushi reports that the measure generated roughly 5 million dollars and extended runway, but it temporarily removed fee flow from xSushi stakers and exposed tension between operational survival and token-holder value capture.","confidence":"high","source_refs":["https://www.sushi.com/blog/kanpai-expires-xsushi-revived","https://www.sushi.com/blog/breaking-down-the-sushi-tokenomics","https://www.coindesk.com/tech/2022/12/07/defi-protocol-sushi-proposes-immediate-action-to-support-its-treasury","https://www.theblock.co/post/204593/sushi-dao-implements-proposal-to-direct-all-trading-fees-to-treasury"]},{"decision":"Soft-launch RouteProcessor2 across fourteen networks before discovery of a critical approval vulnerability.","consequence":"About 1,800 WETH was drained from the largest exposed user before rescue actions. Sushi later committed to make users whole, adding execution and reputation cost during an already weak lifecycle.","confidence":"high","source_refs":["https://www.sushi.com/blog/routeprocessor2-post-mortem","https://www.certik.com/blog/post-mortem-sushiswap"]}],"counterfactual":{"summary":"Earlier leadership continuity, a narrower roadmap, and durable treasury economics could plausibly have preserved more of the initial liquidity advantage. Sushi identifies missing operational efficiency and long-term focus as central problems, but the magnitude of avoided decline cannot be estimated.","confidence":"medium","source_refs":["https://www.sushi.com/blog/introducing-sushi-head-chef-jared-grey","https://www.sushi.com/blog/kanpai-expires-xsushi-revived","https://api.llama.fi/protocol/sushiswap","https://darcyallen.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/02/allen-berg-lane-treasury-governance-dilemma.pdf"]},"watch":[{"signal":"Owned-pool TVL and SushiSwap-adapter volume, kept separate from aggregator-routed volume.","implication":"A sustained owned-liquidity increase would indicate genuine venue recovery. Aggregator growth alone indicates useful routing rather than restoration of the liquidity moat.","source_refs":["https://api.llama.fi/protocol/sushiswap","https://api.llama.fi/summary/dexs/sushiswap?excludeTotalDataChart=false&excludeTotalDataChartBreakdown=false&dataType=dailyVolume"]},{"signal":"Route Processor adoption, integrator volume, and security incidents.","implication":"These determine whether the aggregation pivot creates defensible distribution without recreating router approval risk.","source_refs":["https://www.sushi.com/blog/rp7","https://www.sushi.com/blog/routeprocessor2-post-mortem"]},{"signal":"Treasury runway, fee allocation, and multisig or governance changes.","implication":"These show whether Sushi can fund development while restoring credible value capture and community control.","source_refs":["https://www.sushi.com/blog/kanpai-expires-xsushi-revived","https://www.sushi.com/faq/governance/governance/sushi-governance"]}],"unknowns":["What portion of current routed volume executes in Sushi-owned pools rather than external venues?","What are current treasury assets, liabilities, burn rate, and non-SUSHI runway under a consistent accounting method?","Can the aggregator and API create a durable distribution moat when routing technology is available from larger competitors?","How much of the TVL decline is attributable to governance disruption rather than market and competitive effects?"],"review":{"status":"current","last_reviewed_at":"2026-07-29","next_review_at":"2026-08-05","reviewer":"chaindump-research-desk"}}}',
