  '{"operational_model":"Custodial multi-product centralized exchange offering spot, derivatives, and associated services through jurisdiction-specific entities.","chains":[],"token":{"launched":true,"symbol":"BNB","launch_date":"2017","role":"Exchange-ecosystem utility asset; token existence does not prove that the token caused venue success.","source_url":"https://academy.binance.com/en/articles/what-is-bnb"},"metrics":{"all_product_trading_volume_annual_usd":34000000000000,"users_reported":300000000,"period_end":"2025-12-31","source_url":"https://www.prnewswire.com/in/news-releases/binances-2025-end-of-year-report-trust-liquidity-and-web3-discovery-302657209.html","method_note":"Issuer-reported all-product volume. It cannot be added to spot-only, perpetual-only, or other venue metrics."},"success_factors":["global_liquidity_distribution","broad_product_suite","brand_and_user_distribution","exchange_ecosystem_token"],"risks":["jurisdictional_regulatory_risk","custody_and_counterparty_risk","issuer_reported_metric_scope","bnb_token_value_capture_uncertainty"],"synthesis":"Binance supplies the large-scale centralized-exchange control. It is useful for testing whether distribution and liquidity coincide with survival, but its reported all-product volume is not a like-for-like ranking input against other metric classes.","forensic_analysis":{"version":"forensic-analysis-v1","outcome":{"label":"successful","summary":"Binance is a successful scale control. DOJ identified it as the world''s largest cryptocurrency exchange when it pleaded guilty in 2023; Binance''s issuer report later states $34T of 2025 all-product volume and 300M users. The current figures remain operator-defined, not audited profitability, independent spot volume, or a solvency conclusion.","confidence":"high","as_of":"2025-12-31","source_refs":["binance-2025-report","https://www.justice.gov/criminal/case/united-states-v-binance-holdings-limited-dba-binancecom"]},"why":{"summary":"Binance paired broad global distribution and a wide product suite with deep liquidity and the BNB ecosystem. The observed scale, token utility, and reserve-disclosure surface coexist with success; it remains an inference that any one caused it. Proof of reserves shows selected asset balances and coverage methodology, not all liabilities or corporate solvency.","confidence":"medium","source_refs":["binance-2025-report","binance-bnb","binance-por","https://www.justice.gov/criminal/case/united-states-v-binance-holdings-limited-dba-binancecom","https://www.cftc.gov/PressRoom/PressReleases/8837-23"]},"strategic_choices":[{"confidence":"medium","decision":"Build a global multi-product venue rather than a narrow spot exchange.","consequence":"Users could remain inside one platform across trading and Web3 discovery, increasing distribution leverage while expanding operational and regulatory complexity.","source_refs":["binance-2025-report","https://www.justice.gov/criminal/case/united-states-v-binance-holdings-limited-dba-binancecom","https://www.cftc.gov/PressRoom/PressReleases/8837-23"]},{"confidence":"high","decision":"Launch BNB and expand it from fee utility into a broader chain ecosystem.","consequence":"BNB created retention and ecosystem coordination, but venue and token risks became partially coupled and token success does not prove exchange profitability.","source_refs":["binance-bnb"]},{"confidence":"high","decision":"Publish a proof-of-reserves interface.","consequence":"Users gain an asset-backing checkpoint, while omitted liabilities, entity boundaries, and audit scope prevent a full solvency inference.","source_refs":["binance-por"]}],"counterfactual":{"summary":"A narrow, single-jurisdiction spot strategy could reduce operational and regulatory surface area but sacrifice product breadth, token-network effects, and global distribution. The evidence cannot quantify the marginal contribution of BNB versus liquidity, brand, pricing, or geography.","confidence":"medium","source_refs":["binance-2025-report","binance-bnb","binance-por","https://www.justice.gov/criminal/case/united-states-v-binance-holdings-limited-dba-binancecom","https://www.cftc.gov/PressRoom/PressReleases/8837-23"]},"watch":[{"signal":"Independent spot and derivatives liquidity alongside the operator’s all-product metric.","implication":"Agreement would strengthen the scale thesis; divergence would expose definition or concentration risk.","source_refs":["binance-2025-report"]},{"signal":"Proof-of-reserves scope, frequency, entity coverage, and liability treatment.","implication":"Broader independently tested coverage would strengthen custody evidence without eliminating counterparty risk.","source_refs":["binance-por"]},{"signal":"BNB utility changes and jurisdiction-specific service restrictions.","implication":"Reduced utility or distribution could weaken the ecosystem flywheel attributed to the venue.","source_refs":["binance-bnb","binance-2025-report"]}],"unknowns":["What share of reported volume is spot, derivatives, internal, or incentive-driven?","What are audited revenue, profitability, complete liabilities, and entity-level capital?","How much user retention is attributable to BNB rather than liquidity and price?","How concentrated are users and revenue by jurisdiction and product?"],"review":{"status":"current","last_reviewed_at":"2026-07-29","next_review_at":"2026-08-05","reviewer":"chaindump-research-desk"}}}',
  '[{"id":"binance-2025-report","title":"Binance 2025 End-of-Year Report","publisher":"Binance","url":"https://www.prnewswire.com/in/news-releases/binances-2025-end-of-year-report-trust-liquidity-and-web3-discovery-302657209.html","source_role":"primary","checked_at":"2026-07-29"},{"id":"binance-bnb","title":"What Is BNB?","publisher":"Binance Academy","url":"https://academy.binance.com/en/articles/what-is-bnb","source_role":"primary","checked_at":"2026-07-29"},{"id":"binance-por","title":"Proof of Reserves","publisher":"Binance","url":"https://www.binance.com/en/proof-of-reserves","source_role":"primary","checked_at":"2026-07-29"},{"id":"binance-doj-plea","title":"United States v. Binance Holdings Limited, d/b/a Binance.com","publisher":"U.S. Department of Justice","url":"https://www.justice.gov/criminal/case/united-states-v-binance-holdings-limited-dba-binancecom","source_tier":"T1","source_role":"authority","resolving":true,"evidence_reviewed":true,"evidence_locator":"DOJ records Binance''s guilty plea, $4.3B resolution, then-world-largest exchange status, and its deliberate prioritization of growth, market share, and profit over U.S. compliance controls.","evidence_scope":"legal_and_strategy_finding","checked_at":"2026-07-29","last_verified_at":"2026-07-29","evidence_reviewed_at":"2026-07-29","evidence_reviewer":"codex-research-agent","access_state":"accessible","access_checked_at":"2026-07-29","access_http_status":200,"access_method":"direct_http_retrieval","verification_note":"Direct retrieval returned HTTP 200 and the stated locator was editorially inspected. DOJ records Binance''s guilty plea, $4.3B resolution, then-world-largest exchange status, and its deliberate prioritization of growth, market share, and profit over U.S. compliance controls."},{"id":"binance-cftc-order","title":"Federal Court Enters Order Against Binance and Former CEO, Zhao","publisher":"U.S. Commodity Futures Trading Commission","url":"https://www.cftc.gov/PressRoom/PressReleases/8837-